{ Third visit to the Advance. This time a sly little pawn move, with a plan tucked inside it. } 6. a3 { The point of a3 is b4: chase your queen, grab the queen side. Freeze it: stamp your pawn to c4. [%cal Rb2b4,Yc5c4] } 6... c4 { Frozen. b4 is off the table for good, and b3 is now a hole your knight can visit. [%csl Gb3] } (6... a6 { Playable and calm. } 7. Bd3 { But his b4 plan stays alive. The stamp on c4 kills it. }) (6... a5 { You stop b4 the polite way. } 7. Bd3 { Decent, though the a5 pawn may itch later. The c4 stamp is cleaner. }) (6... Bd7 { Too slow. Watch. } 7. b4 { There is the push, exactly what c4 was meant to deny. }) (6... f6 { A real lever, and playable here. } 7. Bd3 { A different fight. Our plan freezes the queen side first. }) (6... cxd4 { The trade helps him now. } 7. cxd4 { After a3 his b pawn rolls out with gain, and the b2 bishop dreams. }) (6... Nh6 { The old route, one beat late here. } 7. b4 { The space grab arrives for free. c4 was the move to deny it. }) 7. Nbd2 { His knight takes the side door. Send yours touring: a5, heading for that b3 hole. [%cal Yc6a5][%csl Gb3] } 7... Na5 { The knight eyes b3. His queen side squares ache already. } (7... f6 { Also strong. The center lever. } 8. Be2 { Both plans exist. This chapter marches on the queen side. }) (7... Bd7 { First the knight! } 8. b3 { He breaks the clamp at once. Knight to a5 first keeps c4 rock solid. }) (7... Nh6 { The king side can wait. } 8. b3 { Again the clamp cracks. a5 first! }) 8. Be2 { He tidies quietly. Bishop to d7 now. It dreams of a4, trading itself away. [%cal Yc8d7,Bd7a4] } 8... Bd7 (8... Ne7 { Equally good. } 9. h4 { The pieces come in either order. We bring the bishop first. }) (8... h6 { A useful breath. } 9. Rb1 { Never wrong, but the queen side race is the main event. }) 9. Rb1 { He still dreams of b3 someday. Knight to e7: it guards the house and may hop to f5. [%cal Yg8e7] } 9... Ne7 { Set. Push b5 and a5, or castle long and lean in. You call the tune here. [%cal Bb7b5,Ba7a5] } (9... Qc7 { Wise. She steps off the b column early. } 10. Nf1 Nb3 { And look: the knight lands in the hole. Both roads are good. }) (9... O-O-O { Brave and strong. The king joins the storm side. } 10. Qc2 { A rich fight where you press. }) (9... h6 { A fine wait. } 10. h4 { The real business is b5 and a5. }) (9... a6 { Useful someday. } 10. h4 { But the queen side push is the show. }) 0-1


